<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I17ed65968af7a6aaa744febe7f6bff4c0d8bd575" commit="21049782748404bb0fc588054c213ee7f51dd522" commit_message="CHROMIUM: dt-bindings: add dmc-disable-freq property for rockchip dmc  when we disable dmc, we might want to set a specific ddr frequency, so add the dmc-disable-freq property, we can control the ddr frequency when disable dmc.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:43539 TEST=None  Change-Id: I17ed65968af7a6aaa744febe7f6bff4c0d8bd575 Signed-off-by: Lin Huang &lt;hl@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302960 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="302960" owner_email="hl@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/60/302960/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I0e9771da05d0e6c8026b0c0b95a2e40dd1854b75" commit="e1c7a4fed6a039821fb15f80d1d29be3b64a7f96" commit_message="CHROMIUM: rockchip: dmc: add the dmc-disable-freq property  when disable dmc, we might want to set a specific ddr frequency, so add the dmc-disable-freq property, we can control the ddr frequency when disable dmc.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:43539 TEST=ddr run in 433Mhz when disable dmc  Change-Id: I0e9771da05d0e6c8026b0c0b95a2e40dd1854b75 Signed-off-by: Lin Huang &lt;hl@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302961 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="302961" owner_email="hl@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/61/302961/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I645d80aca0edc8af5860889ee5570a684b7113c0" commit="70b3385127ec4458ae2656fccb5a54a7ad6f91b6" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ARM: dts: set dmc-disable-freq to 433Mhz on mickey board  some type of usb speaker will scaccato when play music, ddr scaling frequency seem affect it, so disable dmc, but mickey board sensitive with thermal, and 433Mhz is enough for mickey performance, so set dmc-disable-freq to 433Mhz on mickey board.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:43539 TEST=ddr run in 433Mhz when disable dmc on mickey board  Change-Id: I645d80aca0edc8af5860889ee5570a684b7113c0 Signed-off-by: Lin Huang &lt;hl@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302962 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="302962" owner_email="hl@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/62/302962/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3ae0866d1ff7bb8d0c51355cd6b958310766f19e" commit="fb9c2001a777b305b16da9a81499bd12b510696a" commit_message="charge_state_v2: fix battfake command race condition  This moves battfake console command to the battery driver. This fixes a race condition with using the 'battfake' command where charge_state_v2 could return the real battery percentage even when a faked percentage is specified, if a higher priority task uses the battery state of charge in between when the battery is read, and when the fake state of charge overwrites the battery parameter.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:45878 BRANCH=none TEST=use tap for battery with a faked state of charge. the tap for battery queries the battery percentage a lot, so without this CL, the tap sequence often temporarily jumps to different percentages and colors. with this CL, the tap sequence works great.  Change-Id: I3ae0866d1ff7bb8d0c51355cd6b958310766f19e Signed-off-by: Alec Berg &lt;alecaberg@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302711 Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="302711" owner_email="alecaberg@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/11/302711/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5ae658c8c92469ebc7f516a04bda7b7fbcd32146" commit="9e476e678f1fb1de167eeb4ad4d1256b81424812" commit_message="lightbar: fix battery level hysteresis bug  Fix bug in get_battery_level() where we attempt to apply hysteresis to the battery percentage when it jumps between levels. The problem is if the battery jumps up multiple levels, then it won't always update the battery level. For example, using level thresholds of {14, 40, 99}, if you jump from 0% to 99%, it won't update the battery level because it compares the new percentage, 99%, with the battery threshold for the new level + 1 (100%).  BUG=chrome-os-partner:45878 BRANCH=smaug TEST=use the battfake console command to jump from 5% to 99% and verify that the lightbar goes from all red to google colors. note: without this CL, the lightbar stays all red.  Change-Id: I5ae658c8c92469ebc7f516a04bda7b7fbcd32146 Signed-off-by: Alec Berg &lt;alecaberg@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302684 Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="302684" owner_email="alecaberg@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/84/302684/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2183343b69d01f4835302e291a2e1a0a2c658b1e" commit="6989d9b4dda1ffacc2cfb7ab8c31e3d99b6e4135" commit_message="lightbar: on tap sequence, only get battery percentage once  Change tap sequence so that it only gets the battery percentage once. This means we won't dynamically change color and level if the battery percentage changes mid sequence, but that's ok.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:45878 BRANCH=none TEST=run tap sequence  Change-Id: I2183343b69d01f4835302e291a2e1a0a2c658b1e Signed-off-by: Alec Berg &lt;alecaberg@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302685 Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="302685" owner_email="alecaberg@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/85/302685/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I043d8aea1b8862bc9f309730c241354d980fe9dd" commit="33ab5be744ba175c1e68cd71be3e802006378224" commit_message="CHROMIUM: soc/tegra: pmc: fix the core_osc_time calculation as per TRM  The pulse width should be 122.07uS. Fixed it as per TRM.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:304014 BUG=chrome-os-partner:46124 TEST=LP0 suspend/resume test  Change-Id: I043d8aea1b8862bc9f309730c241354d980fe9dd Signed-off-by: Joseph Lo &lt;josephl@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304013 Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304013" owner_email="josephl@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/13/304013/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I41e94457cd1498e7aff9462fc7c408254cddb663" commit="4d028e515ddfbd32d2fa4ab4fed12ad9aae922c0" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: tegra210: smaug: fix core-pwr-good-time as per TRM.  The pulse width of osc_time should be 122.07uS. Fixed it as per TRM.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:304013 BUG=chrome-os-partner:46124 TEST=LP0 suspend/resume test  Change-Id: I41e94457cd1498e7aff9462fc7c408254cddb663 Signed-off-by: Joseph Lo &lt;josephl@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304014 Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304014" owner_email="josephl@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/14/304014/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.8" change_id="I8ceabfc8d0be94388b76f1b0e288e95bc836e61b" commit="3742156315df95738ee2440601ce8766bd03a7d1" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/exynos: enable render node on exynos.  BUG=chromium:539965 TEST=update_kernel, verify that /dev/dri/renderD128 is present Signed-off-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I8ceabfc8d0be94388b76f1b0e288e95bc836e61b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304322 Commit-Ready: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ilja Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304322" owner_email="hshi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/22/304322/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia28134d5d420f071341217acd3f1fed412c81f7f" commit="fd70b94f5b1cde72093d77ad6bd0c798bcf6c1b2" commit_message="adb_host: Add support for port forwarding.  This adds two new methods for adding and removing port forwarding between an ADB host and a target device, or vice verse (aka reverse forwarding).  BUG=b:24158510 TEST=None  Change-Id: